PATCH 632: resource-open 26fc keeps the variant index and DOS bridge lanes WORD-sized.

Actual original boot 222f calls 26fc for BACKLAND.BIN with DI initially zero
and inherited BP=1718. All three variants fail attribute probes; INC DI visits
0, 1, 2 and reaches the terminator at 3. The original preserves BP, restores the
filename WORD and returns without loader dispatch. Instructions 12706/1270a
operate on 16-bit DI, not a DWORD spanning the adjacent BP bridge lane.

The port read iRam000f000a after a failed probe, combining DI with BP and using
that DWORD as a table index. The reaching regression with the actual filename,
variant bytes and nonzero BP fails on both targets. Keep DI and the DX/SI bridge
writes/readback WORD-sized. The source does not write ES before AH43; preserve
the existing bridge lane instead of overwriting it from an uninitialized C local.
No guessed BP/ES, bounds guard or fallback loader is added.

Source root: scratch/sequence-capture/engine-font-loader/. The actual normal-core
222f -> 26fc -> caller 21a7 snapshots and all 115 boundary records capture three
original AH43 misses, unchanged BP and restored filename. The fixture runs the
real port DOS attribute dispatcher, records consumed WORD operands, and compares
the entire 16-MiB diagnostic memory, including every bridge byte. This does not
establish CPU flags, guest stack, instruction/event integration, successful loader
variants, early vector installation or final frame/PCM parity. Those startup
dependencies remain with 0003/0014/0026; the first event817 difference stays open.
